# Visual QA before next build

After implementing or changing any Figma-backed screen, **do not start the next feature unit** until visual QA passes.

## Required loop

1. Open the **reference frame** (PNG in `design/figma/` or Figma MCP screenshot).
2. Run the app and capture the **implemented screen** (browser screenshot of the real route).
3. Diff structure, copy, spacing, colors, badges, empty states, and key sample data against the frame.
4. **Fix mismatches** before marking the unit done.
5. Only then move to the next build (next route / modal / component group).

## What to check

- Layout regions and order (header → metrics → filters → table / detail columns)
- Exact labels and empty copy from the frame (e.g. “No User Activity”)
- Status / category colors (do not substitute blue for purple, etc.)
- Badge shapes, icon containers (circle vs rounded square), filter chrome (card vs bare)
- Detail hierarchy (e.g. TXN id below title when the frame shows that)

## Docs

Log material Figma ↔ implementation deltas in `context/progress-tracker.md` when intentional (API/data limits) or when fixing.
